ARTICLE I — DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1  "Software" means the Luminex Chess Engine, including but not limited to:
     all source code files, header files, build scripts, configuration files,
     compiled binaries, WebAssembly modules, JavaScript glue code, HTML/CSS
     web assets, documentation, images, logos, branding materials, and any
     other files included in the official distribution or repository.

1.2  "Derivative Work" means any modification, adaptation, translation,
     compilation, or any other form of the Software in which the original
     Software is materially altered, transformed, or built upon, including
     but not limited to: modified source code, recompiled binaries, forked
     versions, integrated products, or any work that incorporates any portion
     of the Software.

1.3  "Distribution" means any act of transferring, publishing, broadcasting,
     hosting, uploading, sharing, or otherwise making the Software or any
     Derivative Work available to any third party by any means, including but
     not limited to: physical media, electronic download, web hosting, API
     access, cloud deployment, or inclusion in any product or service.

1.4  "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is primarily intended
     for or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation,
     including but not limited to:

     (a) Selling, licensing, sublicensing, renting, or leasing the Software
     (b) Incorporating the Software into any product or service that is sold
         or offered for a fee
     (c) Using the Software as part of a subscription service, SaaS platform,
         or pay-to-play gaming service
     (d) Using the Software to generate revenue through advertisements,
         sponsorships, or affiliate links
     (e) Using the Software in a business context for competitive advantage,
         including but not limited to: professional chess training services,
         paid coaching platforms, or commercial chess analysis tools
     (f) Offering the Software as a service (engine-as-a-service) to third
         parties for compensation
     (g) Using the Software in any fundraising, crowdfunding, or
         revenue-sharing arrangement

1.5  "Intellectual Property" means all patents, copyrights, trademarks, trade
     secrets, and any other intellectual property rights associated with the
     Software, whether registered or unregistered.

1.6  "Authorized Recipient" means any individual or entity who has obtained
     a copy of the Software through legitimate means directly from the Licensor
     or from an Authorized Recipient who complied with the distribution terms
     of this License.

