================================================================================
ARTICLE V — ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

5.1  Any use, display, or distribution of the Software must include proper
     attribution to the original authors. Acceptable attribution includes:

     (a) In source code: retaining all original copyright headers and comments
     (b) In compiled binaries: including attribution in accompanying
         documentation or about/version information
     (c) On websites: displaying "Powered by Luminex" or equivalent
         attribution prominently on the page where the engine is used
     (d) In competitions: identifying the engine as "Luminex" with a
         reference to the official repository
     (e) In research papers: citing the Software by name and repository URL

5.2  Attribution must be visible and accessible to end users, not hidden
     in source code alone when the Software is used in a user-facing context.

================================================================================
ARTICLE VI — COMPETITION AND BENCHMARKING
================================================================================

6.1  The Licensee may enter the Software in chess engine competitions
     (tournaments, rating lists, benchmarks, and similar events) provided:

     (a) The engine participates under its official name "Luminex"
     (b) No misrepresentation of the engine's identity, origin, or strength
     (c) The competition organizers are provided with accurate information
         about the Software and its license terms
     (d) The participation does not involve any Commercial Use
     (e) The Licensee complies with all rules and regulations of the
         competition

6.2  The Licensee may not:

     (a) Submit the Software under a different name
     (b) Claim the Software as their own creation without attribution
     (c) Use the Software to gain unfair advantage in human chess competitions

================================================================================
ARTICLE VII — ONLINE AND WEB DEPLOYMENT
================================================================================

7.1  The WebAssembly version of the Software may be deployed on websites
     under the following conditions:

     (a) The deployment must be non-commercial as defined in Section 1.4
     (b) The website must be freely accessible to all users without payment,
         registration walls, or mandatory data collection
     (c) Proper attribution must be displayed on the page where the engine
         is used, including the name "Luminex" and a link to the official
         repository when feasible
     (d) The deployed files must not be obfuscated or modified to obscure
         their origin
     (e) The Licensee must not claim ownership of the engine or imply
         official endorsement by the Licensor

7.2  Web deployment must not:

     (a) Expose the engine as a public API for commercial use by third parties
     (b) Be embedded in any commercial product, iframe, or wrapper that
         generates revenue
     (c) Be deployed in any manner that exceeds reasonable usage limits or
         imposes excessive load on the Licensor's infrastructure (if any)

